1
00:00:16,029 --> 00:00:19,868
<i>SAWYER FARM
ESTABLISHED 1845

2
00:00:21,494 --> 00:00:30,548
<i># Happy birthday to you...

3
00:00:30,672 --> 00:00:35,513
<i># Happy birthday, dear Jed...

4
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:40,434
<i># Happy birthday to you...

5
00:00:40,559 --> 00:00:42,271
All right, now make a wish.

6
00:00:42,306 --> 00:00:43,273
Blow them out.

7
00:00:48,068 --> 00:00:50,321
Yes! Very good!

8
00:00:50,362 --> 00:00:52,532
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

9
00:00:52,573 --> 00:00:53,784
Very good!

10
00:00:53,908 --> 00:00:55,202
All right...

11
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:01,086
Drayton, where are your manners?

12
00:01:01,169 --> 00:01:03,338
Give the first slice to the thief.

13
00:01:18,105 --> 00:01:19,586
I didn't steal your damn pigs...

14
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:21,068
Are you calling my son a liar?

15
00:01:21,193 --> 00:01:23,446
He saw your filthy hands stealing our property...

16
00:01:28,032 --> 00:01:30,829
Why would I go anywhere near your filthy pigs?

17
00:01:30,953 --> 00:01:32,415
Or your filthy family!

18
00:01:32,498 --> 00:01:35,585
I swear, everybody will know what kind of...

19
00:01:35,626 --> 00:01:37,504
...offspring you're raising here, Verna!

20
00:01:37,586 --> 00:01:39,423
Shut him up! I've had enough!

21
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:42,933
Listen to me, no farmhand is going to...

22
00:01:42,968 --> 00:01:44,764
...ruin my son's special night.

23
00:01:48,017 --> 00:01:49,394
Ready for your present?

24
00:01:52,689 --> 00:01:54,692
You know you're my special boy.

25
00:01:55,275 --> 00:01:57,362
Come on, Jed. There you go...

26
00:02:00,199 --> 00:02:02,452
- Jed.
- Yes, that's it, Jed.

27
00:02:04,955 --> 00:02:05,999
Now remember,

28
00:02:06,207 --> 00:02:09,336
bad people like him try to destroy our family.

29
00:02:09,961 --> 00:02:11,756
But we won't let that happen, will we?

30
00:02:11,922 --> 00:02:13,298
Go on, pick it up...

31
00:02:14,091 --> 00:02:15,593
Jed, pick it up...

32
00:02:16,134 --> 00:02:16,970
Jed!

33
00:02:17,094 --> 00:02:20,723
Jed...

34
00:02:20,764 --> 00:02:22,310
Pick it up, Jed!

35
00:02:22,351 --> 00:02:25,647
Jed!

36
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,441
Come on, you know what you have to do...

37
00:02:28,858 --> 00:02:30,571
That's it, Jed!

38
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:33,991
Come on, Jed...

39
00:02:34,699 --> 00:02:37,537
Jed!

40
00:02:37,619 --> 00:02:39,080
No!

41
00:02:39,121 --> 00:02:40,374
There you go.

42
00:02:40,790 --> 00:02:42,042
Go on, son!

43
00:02:42,077 --> 00:02:43,378
No!

44
00:02:50,092 --> 00:02:51,804
No!

45
00:02:57,394 --> 00:02:59,481
No!

46
00:02:59,647 --> 00:03:01,483
No, please!

47
00:03:01,608 --> 00:03:04,403
No!

48
00:03:04,444 --> 00:03:07,073
Do it, do it, do it!

49
00:03:07,114 --> 00:03:09,075
No!

50
00:03:09,116 --> 00:03:10,827
Go on, Jed, do it...

51
00:03:11,786 --> 00:03:12,830
Do it!

52
00:03:13,414 --> 00:03:15,626
- Jed.
- Do it!

53
00:03:21,923 --> 00:03:23,051
Mom!

54
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,094
Mom, no!

55
00:03:26,846 --> 00:03:30,185
No!

56
00:03:40,071 --> 00:03:40,906
Hey.

57
00:03:41,197 --> 00:03:42,784
You let us down, Jed.

58
00:03:45,536 --> 00:03:48,623
It's all right. Family will always be here for
you.

59
00:03:48,789 --> 00:03:50,124
Remember that.

60
00:03:50,875 --> 00:03:51,918
All right.

61
00:04:09,606 --> 00:04:14,697
<i>TEXAS, 1955

62
00:04:17,698 --> 00:04:19,119
Are you trying to get us killed?

63
00:04:19,159 --> 00:04:20,036
Do you want me to stop?

64
00:04:20,078 --> 00:04:21,329
No, I didn't say that.

65
00:04:28,630 --> 00:04:29,716
Watch out!

66
00:04:34,429 --> 00:04:36,225
What the hell was that thing?

67
00:04:37,516 --> 00:04:38,728
Hey, Betty.

68
00:04:45,943 --> 00:04:47,195
What is it?

69
00:04:48,487 --> 00:04:49,615
I don't know.

70
00:04:52,868 --> 00:04:54,330
Then let's go.

71
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:04,592
What?

72
00:05:12,976 --> 00:05:14,312
He's just a kid!

73
00:05:16,356 --> 00:05:17,650
Let's go!

74
00:05:18,024 --> 00:05:19,443
We'll be late.

75
00:05:21,570 --> 00:05:23,072
Hello.

76
00:05:27,328 --> 00:05:28,622
Are you okay?

77
00:05:34,753 --> 00:05:36,798
You shouldn't play in the road.

78
00:05:36,964 --> 00:05:38,925
Help me, please...

79
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:47,061
Hey, Betty, where are you going? I didn't hit him!

80
00:05:47,477 --> 00:05:49,105
- Something's wrong.
- Betty!

81
00:05:49,145 --> 00:05:50,565
He needs help.

82
00:05:51,107 --> 00:05:52,525
Jesus Christ!

83
00:05:56,947 --> 00:05:58,909
Hey, buddy, can you hear me?

84
00:06:00,911 --> 00:06:02,454
Let me help you!

85
00:06:06,332 --> 00:06:07,501
Hello?

86
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:16,722
It's okay. You can come out.

87
00:06:18,179 --> 00:06:19,308
Betty.

88
00:06:23,103 --> 00:06:24,814
Betty, where did you go?

89
00:07:23,094 --> 00:07:24,389
Hello?

90
00:07:29,561 --> 00:07:33,107
Come on... I won't hurt you.

91
00:07:35,650 --> 00:07:37,153
I just want to help...

92
00:07:44,203 --> 00:07:45,372
Okay?

93
00:07:56,261 --> 00:08:00,558
<i>BASED ON CHARACTERS CREATED BY

94
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:03,604
<i>KIM HENKEL AND TOBE HOOPER

95
00:08:05,897 --> 00:08:07,941
You did good, Jed!

96
00:08:08,733 --> 00:08:11,779
It's like... I can still feel you in there
after all.

97
00:08:43,107 --> 00:08:46,696
Well, let him learn a little more.

98
00:08:50,157 --> 00:08:51,702
Oh, my God!

99
00:09:01,338 --> 00:09:02,257
Show him!

100
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:16,857
- Where is she?
- Calm down, Hal.

101
00:09:17,357 --> 00:09:18,944
Let me through, damn it!

102
00:09:18,985 --> 00:09:20,530
Let me go! Let me go, damn it!

103
00:09:20,570 --> 00:09:22,155
- We know what happened.
- Calm down, Hal.

104
00:09:22,321 --> 00:09:23,950
Is that my little girl in there?

105
00:09:25,451 --> 00:09:28,330
Is she in there? Is my little girl in there?

106
00:09:28,664 --> 00:09:30,041
Answer me, damn it!

107
00:09:30,374 --> 00:09:31,751
We've got one of them.

108
00:09:36,130 --> 00:09:37,509
Oh, boy!

109
00:09:41,679 --> 00:09:43,057
I couldn't get to her in time!

110
00:09:43,265 --> 00:09:45,310
I'm so sorry, sir. I swear to God.

111
00:09:47,811 --> 00:09:49,522
Drayton Sawyer...

112
00:09:52,024 --> 00:09:53,903
It's time to go to Gorman Reformatory.

113
00:09:53,944 --> 00:09:57,283
No... You're all grown up now.

114
00:09:59,534 --> 00:10:01,538
That means the gas chamber for you.

115
00:10:05,208 --> 00:10:06,462
Why?

116
00:10:06,794 --> 00:10:08,631
Are you going to arrest me for finding a dead
body?

117
00:10:08,838 --> 00:10:10,300
Last I checked, that wasn't a crime.

118
00:10:10,349 --> 00:10:13,103
How about a bullet hole in your damn skull?

119
00:10:13,769 --> 00:10:15,069
- Put it away, Hal.
- Come on.

120
00:10:15,104 --> 00:10:16,982
He's right. We've got nothing on him...

121
00:10:17,356 --> 00:10:18,565
Calm down, Hal.

122
00:10:18,773 --> 00:10:19,525
Keep your head clear.

123
00:10:19,565 --> 00:10:22,069
- Hal, it's not worth it.
- Come on, Hal, lower the gun.

124
00:10:22,193 --> 00:10:23,529
Damn trash.

125
00:10:34,705 --> 00:10:36,666
Let those boys go right this instant!

126
00:10:36,957 --> 00:10:38,626
Don't count on it, Verna!

127
00:10:39,376 --> 00:10:40,837
Do you think they did anything wrong?

128
00:10:40,877 --> 00:10:41,963
No, I don't!

129
00:10:42,045 --> 00:10:43,881
You bastard, let them out of the car!

130
00:10:44,381 --> 00:10:47,176
No! They're going to stay there and rot!

131
00:10:48,259 --> 00:10:49,344
On what charges?

132
00:10:49,635 --> 00:10:50,929
They're not under arrest.

133
00:10:50,970 --> 00:10:53,265
They're in protective custody... from you.

134
00:10:53,306 --> 00:10:54,558
What are you talking about?

135
00:10:55,558 --> 00:10:58,103
I can't count how many crime scenes I've been
to...

136
00:10:58,144 --> 00:11:00,481
...where there's always a Sawyer involved.

137
00:11:01,023 --> 00:11:02,816
Those boys aren't safe with you...

138
00:11:02,898 --> 00:11:04,026
Bullshit.

139
00:11:04,942 --> 00:11:07,280
Get a warrant for the Sawyer house.

140
00:11:07,612 --> 00:11:09,657
Name every one of them. I want them all.

141
00:11:09,823 --> 00:11:10,825
- Did you hear me?
- You can't do that.

142
00:11:10,907 --> 00:11:11,784
You can't do that!

143
00:11:11,867 --> 00:11:13,578
Well, by the time we get there, I'll have a
warrant saying I can...

144
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:15,121
...do just that.

145
00:11:15,787 --> 00:11:17,914
It's called "children at risk."

146
00:11:19,332 --> 00:11:21,293
You took one of mine...

147
00:11:22,043 --> 00:11:24,463
...so I'll take every one of yours, Verna.

148
00:11:30,635 --> 00:11:32,011
Every last one of them...

149
00:11:34,013 --> 00:11:36,016
<i>10 YEARS LATER

150
00:11:36,474 --> 00:11:40,145
<i>In 1935, the state of Texas established a...

151
00:11:40,186 --> 00:11:42,689
<i>...program to care for children at risk.

152
00:11:42,855 --> 00:11:46,193
In its first year, nearly 52 children were
removed from homes...

153
00:11:46,274 --> 00:11:49,111
...known to be involved in criminal activity.

154
00:11:49,444 --> 00:11:52,324
<i>Many of these children were given new names...

155
00:11:52,365 --> 00:11:54,159
<i>...and placed in foster homes.

156
00:11:54,283 --> 00:11:57,871
<i>Others, products of degenerate parenting...

157
00:11:57,912 --> 00:12:00,749
<i>...ended up here at Gorman Reformatory.

158
00:12:00,790 --> 00:12:02,165
<i>GORMAN HOUSE JUVENILE REFORMATORY

159
00:12:02,206 --> 00:12:06,336
We take care of their physical and
psychological needs.

160
00:12:06,794 --> 00:12:08,047
Yes, sir.

161
00:12:08,171 --> 00:12:10,967
I've wanted to come here for a long time.

162
00:12:11,257 --> 00:12:12,593
I think I can help them.

163
00:12:12,759 --> 00:12:13,803
Elizabeth.

164
00:12:13,843 --> 00:12:15,471
Please, sir, Lizzy. Lizzy is fine.

165
00:12:15,512 --> 00:12:17,013
Elizabeth.

166
00:12:17,972 --> 00:12:20,225
Most of these children will end up...

167
00:12:20,265 --> 00:12:22,477
...in prisons or mental institutions.

168
00:12:23,519 --> 00:12:26,983
Keeping them here makes everyone safer.

169
00:12:27,774 --> 00:12:29,026
Keep your guard up.

170
00:13:13,694 --> 00:13:15,071
Well... hello...

171
00:13:15,904 --> 00:13:17,365
My name is Lizzy.

172
00:13:17,448 --> 00:13:20,327
I'm new here, and I'd like to get to know you.

173
00:13:24,872 --> 00:13:26,207
That's Bud.

174
00:13:27,833 --> 00:13:30,209
He doesn't say much for such a big guy.

175
00:13:35,632 --> 00:13:36,634
You're in my seat.

176
00:13:37,175 --> 00:13:38,344
I'm sorry.

177
00:13:39,218 --> 00:13:41,221
- Very nice.
- I'm...

178
00:13:41,262 --> 00:13:43,307
Lizzy... Yeah, I heard. I heard.

179
00:13:44,306 --> 00:13:46,476
Shit, sorry. I'm Jackson.

180
00:13:47,267 --> 00:13:50,230
Jackson and... Bud...

181
00:13:51,022 --> 00:13:53,484
And what medication are you taking, Jackson?

182
00:13:53,650 --> 00:13:54,860
Medication?

183
00:13:56,069 --> 00:13:58,030
They already gave it to us when they brought
us in, right?

184
00:13:59,029 --> 00:14:01,949
We figured you'd know more about that than we
do, Lizzy...

185
00:14:02,949 --> 00:14:05,371
You're not going to give me any trouble, are you?

186
00:14:05,870 --> 00:14:07,331
No, not me, Lizzy.

187
00:14:08,665 --> 00:14:09,964
Is there a reason you keep...

188
00:14:09,999 --> 00:14:11,543
...saying my name like that?

189
00:14:12,126 --> 00:14:16,380
No... I just like to know who's in charge,
that's all.

190
00:14:19,465 --> 00:14:21,135
Fuck you, asshole!

191
00:14:21,176 --> 00:14:22,095
I'll kick your ass.

192
00:14:22,135 --> 00:14:23,888
I'll fuck up your head!

193
00:14:24,012 --> 00:14:25,098
Let him go!

194
00:14:25,138 --> 00:14:26,683
Mind your own business!

195
00:14:26,807 --> 00:14:28,190
It is my business.

196
00:14:28,225 --> 00:14:29,643
What's the problem?

197
00:14:30,142 --> 00:14:32,562
He said something I didn't like.

198
00:14:32,853 --> 00:14:36,358
About what a girl in a nurse's uniform would
taste like.

199
00:14:37,233 --> 00:14:38,820
Hey, hey, let go of me!

200
00:14:39,111 --> 00:14:40,488
Let go!

201
00:14:41,321 --> 00:14:42,907
Fuck you, Frankenstein!

202
00:14:42,948 --> 00:14:44,574
That's enough. Stop it.

203
00:14:44,949 --> 00:14:47,370
- Ike, what did you do?
- I didn't do anything.

204
00:14:50,414 --> 00:14:51,624
Everything's fine.

205
00:15:52,599 --> 00:15:54,226
What are you doing?

206
00:15:59,188 --> 00:16:00,482
Come here.

207
00:16:03,818 --> 00:16:05,321
What's the problem?

208
00:16:05,362 --> 00:16:07,198
It's just a stupid mouse.

209
00:16:10,075 --> 00:16:11,369
Got a light?

210
00:16:11,451 --> 00:16:13,286
You know smoking isn't allowed in here...

211
00:16:15,579 --> 00:16:17,958
I have special permission.

212
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:20,002
True story.

213
00:16:20,043 --> 00:16:21,963
Ask Dr. Lang.

214
00:16:22,170 --> 00:16:23,005
I will.

215
00:16:23,046 --> 00:16:25,007
He'll tell you it helps me.

216
00:16:26,091 --> 00:16:28,717
With my anxiety.

217
00:16:31,970 --> 00:16:33,514
The truth is...

218
00:16:34,555 --> 00:16:36,685
...it's because I'm his favorite.

219
00:16:37,059 --> 00:16:38,521
He told me so.

220
00:16:38,728 --> 00:16:41,398
- You've earned yourself a warning.
- Why?

221
00:16:41,438 --> 00:16:42,983
I was just taking a bath.

222
00:16:43,023 --> 00:16:44,359
Get out.

223
00:16:47,778 --> 00:16:49,072
Bitch.

224
00:16:50,906 --> 00:16:52,660
Is everything all right?

225
00:16:53,368 --> 00:16:55,579
Yes, Doctor, I'm fine.

226
00:16:56,161 --> 00:17:01,042
I'll handle Isaac and Bud.

227
00:17:01,125 --> 00:17:02,877
No. Bud didn't do anything.

228
00:17:02,918 --> 00:17:05,317
I look forward to our session tomorrow, Jackson.

229
00:17:05,352 --> 00:17:07,716
I'm sorry, but he's actually right.

230
00:17:07,756 --> 00:17:09,051
Bud didn't do anything.

231
00:17:09,092 --> 00:17:11,218
He was fighting...

232
00:17:11,843 --> 00:17:13,512
Well, he was protecting me...

233
00:17:13,594 --> 00:17:14,847
Remind me to tell you later what...

234
00:17:14,887 --> 00:17:16,473
...he did to his last foster family.

235
00:17:16,556 --> 00:17:18,225
Well, they took his dog away.

236
00:17:18,766 --> 00:17:22,062
Yes... that's a perfectly good reason...

237
00:17:22,103 --> 00:17:24,732
...to put someone in a coma.

238
00:17:25,107 --> 00:17:26,608
Well, I'm just saying.

239
00:17:49,046 --> 00:17:49,964
<i>DIAGNOSIS: BIPOLAR DISORDER

240
00:17:50,005 --> 00:17:53,926
<i>Upon admission, this 16-year-old boy,
Horton, Bud, was depressed, agitated and
fearful.

241
00:17:54,051 --> 00:17:57,094
<i>Overall, his behavior was aggressive,
unusually energetic and withdrawn.

242
00:18:00,306 --> 00:18:02,142
Sorry, I didn't mean to scare you.

243
00:18:02,892 --> 00:18:04,227
You didn't.

244
00:18:04,977 --> 00:18:06,563
Thank you for helping Bud.

245
00:18:07,647 --> 00:18:11,275
I know you don't even know him, so that was nice.

246
00:18:12,025 --> 00:18:14,945
Well, I'm here to help you all. So...

247
00:18:16,697 --> 00:18:18,992
You're the first pretty nurse we've had around
here.

248
00:18:21,869 --> 00:18:23,455
So I thought you should know...

249
00:18:24,956 --> 00:18:26,124
Know what?

250
00:18:26,457 --> 00:18:29,087
What goes on in the relaxation room...

251
00:18:30,003 --> 00:18:31,882
The kids around here call it...

252
00:18:32,048 --> 00:18:34,301
...Dr. Lang's chamber of horrors.

253
00:18:34,717 --> 00:18:36,303
Piece of shit.

254
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:38,138
Why is that?

255
00:18:38,513 --> 00:18:41,014
Go there at night and find out for yourself...

256
00:18:42,556 --> 00:18:45,060
Hey, you might even do something about it.

257
00:18:46,435 --> 00:18:47,521
You know.

258
00:18:48,689 --> 00:18:49,816
Jackson...

259
00:18:52,109 --> 00:18:54,277
You'll get out of here one day.

260
00:18:54,568 --> 00:18:57,197
And just because you can't trust certain people...

261
00:18:58,698 --> 00:19:00,826
...doesn't mean you shouldn't trust others.

262
00:19:01,909 --> 00:19:03,537
Well, I'll think about it.

263
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,419
<i>DR. LANG

264
00:19:15,006 --> 00:19:16,508
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

265
00:19:16,590 --> 00:19:19,261
Barry Farnsworth, we had an appointment an
hour ago.

266
00:19:19,343 --> 00:19:20,762
Did we?

267
00:19:23,056 --> 00:19:24,598
Mrs. Sawyer.

268
00:19:24,764 --> 00:19:26,934
It's Mrs. Carson now.

269
00:19:33,023 --> 00:19:34,608
I want to see Jed.

270
00:19:34,941 --> 00:19:37,028
We've been through this before.

271
00:19:37,527 --> 00:19:38,904
Year after year...

272
00:19:38,945 --> 00:19:40,281
He's my son.

273
00:19:40,697 --> 00:19:42,325
And I can afford a lawyer now.

274
